Thanks, Keren, for the detailed investigation — good catch. You’re right that we should use the kStandalone display mode to better reflect real PWA remote cocoa scenarios.

I’ve updated the test to use `kStandalone` and replaced `SendKeyPressSync` with `FindBarController::EndFindSession` to close the Find bar, this works for both PWA and normal browser windows. And I’m now able to reproduce the issue in the PWA test without RWHVMac changes as shown below. Please take a look at the latest changes when you have a chance. Thanks again!

1. Open Find bar
`ASSERT_TRUE(base::test::RunUntil(
      [&]() { return focus_tracker.lost_focus_count() == 2; }));`

2. Close Find bar
`ASSERT_TRUE(base::test::RunUntil([&]() {
    return focus_tracker.focused_count() == 2 && 
    focus_tracker.lost_focus_count() == 1;
  }));`

